Step-by-step plan
Step	What I did	Done when
1. Read the brief	Listed the pages, features and marking criteria	I had a checklist of every requirement
2. Design	Made Login, Register, Home, Add item popup and Profile screens in Figma	All four pages and the popup were designed
3. Set up	Created a Vite + React + TypeScript project and installed Redux Toolkit, React Router, bcryptjs, json-server and react-hot-toast	npm run dev and npm run server both ran
4. Plan the state	Decided where each kind of data lives (see the table below)	Every piece of data had one home
5. Types and store	Wrote the TypeScript types, userSlice, listsSlice and the store	The app loaded with no type errors
6. Routing	Added public and protected routes with a shared layout	Logged-out users could not open Home or Profile
7. Authentication	Built Register and Login with bcrypt hashing	db.json showed hashed passwords
8. Shopping list CRUD	Built add, view, edit and delete for lists and items, with the Add item popup	Changes were saved to json-server and survived a refresh
9. Search, sort and filter	Stored search, sort and category in the URL with useSearchParams	Editing the URL changed the page
10. Profile	Built a view mode and an edit mode for personal and login details	Changes were saved and shown across the app
11. Sharing	Let an owner share a list by email, shown read-only to the other user	The second user saw the list under "Shared with you"
12. Extras	Added strong password rules, forgot password, a show/hide password eye and list renaming	Each one worked and was tested
13. Styling	Applied the Figma design and made it responsive	Checked at 320, 480, 768 and 1024px
14. Test	Walked through every feature, and fixed bugs	No errors in the Problems panel or the browser console
15. Document and submit	Wrote the README and this document, then opened a pull request	Pull request sent to my mentor
Where each kind of state lives
Kind of state	Where it lives	Why
Logged-in user	Redux (userSlice) and localStorage	Many components need it, and it must survive a refresh
Shopping lists and shared lists	Redux (listsSlice), saved in json-server	Many components need them
Search, sort and category	The URL	Shareable, bookmarkable, survives a refresh
Form drafts, open popups, saving flags	useState	Only one component needs them
